  "proposal": {
    "hypothesis": "Failures stem from two general defects: (1) the RAG scorer ranks by raw overlap only, so an untrusted high-overlap document (trusted=0, overlap=1.0) outranks the trusted authoritative source, causing wrong/UNKNOWN answers and wrong evidence citations; (2) the retry expression is a constant 0, so transient (retryable) tool errors are never retried, and permanent errors are not distinguished. Fixing RAG scoring to weight trust/scope/entity/recency and making retry a function of error_retryable and attempt count should recover authority selection and transient-error recovery without touching policy.",
